From 9b862e9c9d6f4821b7e4af9a8a08444581e62d0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 15:18:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] video: sun5i-eink: Write the palette to the pipe0 palette
 table

The layer palette for the Index working mode lives in the per-pipe
palette tables at BE+0x5000 (pipe0) / BE+0x5400 (pipe1), per the A13
user manual DEBE memory map. 0x4400 is the gamma table - the palette
was being uploaded there and the pipe0 table scanned out garbage,
which is why the panel never reacted in the indexed format. The
vendor epdc.ko also writes 0x5000 (the earlier 0x4400 reading of the
decompiled code was a decode error).

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/video/fbdev/sun5i-eink.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/video/fbdev/sun5i-eink.c b/drivers/video/fbdev/sun5i-eink.c
index 08ec526944d5..bbaa28657c6b 100644
--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/sun5i-eink.c
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/sun5i-eink.c
@@ -139,8 +139,12 @@
 #define SUN4I_BACKEND_LAY_FBFMT_8BPP				(3 << 8)
 #define SUN4I_BACKEND_LAY_FBFMT_XRGB8888			(9 << 8)
 
-/* 256 x u32 palette RAM for <=8bpp layer formats */
-#define SUN4I_BACKEND_PALETTE_REG		0x4400
+/*
+ * 256 x u32 pipe0 palette table, used by layers in the Index working
+ * mode. NOT at 0x4400 - that's the gamma table; the layer palette
+ * tables are per pipe: pipe0 0x5000-0x53ff, pipe1 0x5400-0x57ff.
+ */
+#define SUN4I_BACKEND_PALETTE_REG		0x5000
 
 // }}}
 
